{
  "requirement": "[`Sources`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/sources/struct.Sources.html) supplies\nbuilt-in filesystem listing, reading, outlining, text search, and structural\nsearch. Construct it with the project directory:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::sources::Sources;\n\nlet sources = Sources::new(repository_root);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.provider` has two obligations. `Sources` must supply built-in listing, reading, outlining, text search and structural search. It must also be constructible with `Sources::new(repository_root)`. I did not request implementation source. The supplied tests cover both obligations.\n\n- **Construction:** `Sources::new(root.path())` is called on a real temporary directory in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]`. It runs with and without a Git repository. The same call appears in `#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]`.\n- **Listing:** `sources.list` is asserted to include `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`. It is asserted to exclude ignored files, `skip/` and `.git/`. Listing a specific excluded path returns an empty result.\n- **Reading:** `sources.read` succeeds for `.gitignore`. It fails for ignored files and for `.git/config`.\n- **Outlining:** `sources.parse` is asserted to fail for ignored files. In `#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]`, `parse` on `note.unknown` yields the `plain-text-structural-v1` scheme and an outline with 3 items. `parse` on `visible.rs` yields the `rust-structural-v1` scheme under the `default-languages` feature.\n- **Text search:** `sources.search_text` is checked with a literal and a regex pattern, each expecting 3 matches. Scoped searches over excluded prefixes return nothing. A `..` scope is an error. The scope `./src/../src` resolves to `src/nested.txt`.\n- **Structural search:** `sources.search_structure` is asserted to return one match at `visible.rs`. Scopes `hidden.rs`, `skip` and `.git` return no matches. Scope `..` is an error. Without the `default-languages` feature, the search is an error.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` also exercises the provider's parse, outline and text-search defaults. It uses an in-memory provider rather than `Sources`.\n\nAll five capabilities are exercised on the real `Sources` type with outcome assertions. No gap found.",
